+      `${intro} supplier has offered the requested stem with barge nomination subject to final terminal approval. Please check whether the receiving vessel can accept delivery alongside cargo operations without affecting ETD ${etdDate}.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} please ensure the bunker delivery note shows density, sulphur, viscosity, and sample seal numbers. We need the certificate before sailing for emissions reporting and charterparty records.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} commercial approval is granted at the nominated quantity, provided no waiting time applies before the confirmed delivery window. Please revert immediately if the barge loses the slot.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} noted and filed. Please send the final BDN scan after completion and copy performance analytics for consumption reconciliation.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`
+    ],
+    charterparty_revision: [
+      `${intro}\n\nPlease review the proposed charterparty revision for ${voyage.vessel_name} / ${voyage.voyage_id}. The main changes cover laycan wording, EU ETS cost allocation, and documentary responsibilities between ${voyage.origin_port} and ${voyage.destination_port}.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} we can accept the revised cargo description as ${voyage.cargo}, but the demurrage exception language needs to remain narrow and tied to terminal-caused delay only.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} please amend clause 18 so MRV and emissions evidence are provided within five business days after completion of discharge. This avoids a reporting gap if the voyage closes after month end.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} the freight calculation ties with the fixture recap after adjusting for the revised load quantity of ${qty}. Please confirm the final rider page before we release clean copies.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} clean copy is approved subject to the last wording change on laytime exceptions. Please mark this version as the operative synthetic demo fixture for ${voyage.voyage_id}.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`
+    ],
+    eta_delay: [
+      `${intro}\n\n${voyage.vessel_name} is now forecasting a delayed ETA at ${voyage.destination_port}. Current ETA is ${etaDate}; the delay is driven by reduced speed on the previous leg and precautionary routing. Cargo remains ${voyage.cargo}.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} please alert the terminal and receivers that the berthing request may need to move to the next tide window. We are still inside the operational tolerance but should protect against standby charges.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} master reports weather improving and intends to recover part of the delay if consumption remains within charterparty limits. We will not order higher speed without commercial approval.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} revised ETA has been passed to the agent. Please keep demurrage exposure under review if berth readiness is withdrawn before arrival.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} latest noon position supports the revised ETA. No further escalation unless the delay exceeds 12 hours or terminal cancels the berth nomination.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`
+    ],
+    port_congestion: [
+      `${intro}\n\nThe agent reports congestion at ${voyage.destination_port} for ${voyage.vessel_name}. Current line-up shows two vessels ahead for the relevant berth, with possible waiting time on arrival under ${voyage.voyage_id}.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
+      `${intro} please confirm whether NOR can be tendered at anchorage if berth is unavailable. The local agent believes tendering is permitted after free pratique by radio, but we need charterparty alignment.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
