      `${intro} berth prospects improved slightly, but there remains a risk of overnight anchorage. Please keep agency proformas separate for waiting-time items so finance can review them clearly.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
      `${intro} understood. We will maintain the current port rotation and avoid diverting unless the berth delay exceeds the receiver's tolerance window.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`
    ],
    eu_ets_exposure: [
      `${intro}\n\nPlease see the EU ETS exposure estimate for ${voyage.vessel_name} on ${voyage.voyage_id}. The synthetic calculation covers the leg from ${voyage.origin_port} to ${voyage.destination_port} and uses provisional fuel consumption pending final noon data.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
      `${intro} the current estimate allocates emissions by voyage leg and assumes standard EU scope treatment for the fictional trade lane. Please confirm whether the charterer or owner account should carry the allowance booking.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
      `${intro} finance needs the allowance exposure split before month close. The largest sensitivity is actual speed after departure ${etdDate}; please update if the vessel is instructed to increase RPM.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
      `${intro} noted on the allowance booking. We will hold the accrual at the provisional estimate and true it up once MRV fuel figures are complete.${attachmentLine}${signoff}`,
